# The only tools a skill marked headless: true may list in headless-tools, one per line.
# bin/harness refuses a skill whose list names anything else, and tests/test_skills.py
# checks every entry here only reads. Only bin/harness reads headless-tools: Claude Code's
# own allowed-tools would apply in every session the skill runs in, so a skill never puts a
# Bash rule there. An entry belongs here only if it can't run a program, write a file or
# reach a host of its own choosing, whatever flags follow it, in a run the guard holds.
# Adding one is a reviewed change to this file.
#
# No Bash rule is safe on its own: `gh pr view -R <host>/...` reaches any host, checked
# 2026-10-25, and with Bash among a run's tools a person's own Bash allow rules apply too.
# The Bash entries below are safe headless because .claude/hooks/guard.py refuses every
# command in a headless run except `gh pr view <n>`, `gh pr diff <n>` and `gh issue view <n>`.
# Read, Grep and Glob are safe headless because the guard holds their paths, and a Glob's
# pattern, inside the harness root.
Read
Grep
Glob
Bash(gh pr view:*)
Bash(gh pr diff:*)
Bash(gh issue view:*)
